//
// `@FR-Disp-Dynamic` crossed with `@FR-M-Exhaust`: a set that misses a variant and has no
// enum-level member would be a non-exhaustive canonical `match`, so the enum-held call is a
// static refusal at the call — never a run-time "no applicable method" — exactly where the
// written-out match with the same arms is refused.  This file holds one refusal: the call
// misses `C` and `D`.  (The message names the first uncovered variant; M-Exhaust's names both.)
//
// CHANNEL: the compile (the expected diagnostic).
// Every cell held on both backends when written; the ledger rows are in
// doc/claude/RULE_CROSSINGS-history.md.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `dm(K)` has no definition for the variant (C) — declared: dm(A), dm(B)

enum K { A { n: integer }, B { n: integer }, C { n: integer }, D { n: integer } }

fn dm(a: A) -> text { "a{a.n}" }
fn dm(a: B) -> text { "b{a.n}" }

fn main() {
  println(dm(A { n: 0 }));
  x: K = B { n: 1 };
  println(dm(x));
}
